  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support of The Young Entrepreneur Programme Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ethiopian private sector faces several challenges in attracting and educating local managers. Actual management skills and learning-by-doing are not an integral part of the formal education system. As a result, employers face ambitious employees who lack a solid theoretical and practical base to perform a management position within the company.The Young Entrepreneur Programme (YEP) fills this niche by providing young employees with management and entrepreneurial knowledge and skills which they directly apply in their jobs or within the companies they are employed by. As a result of the acquired skills and knowledge, participants improve their professional and personal performance and deliver improved quality of service. Employers do completely cover the participation of employees. This project supports YEP&apos;s expansion strategy to attract more participants and strengthen its education portfolio further. As such, this project contributes to skills development in the Ethiopian labour market, decreasing the need to import knowledge and experience from abroad.</narrative>
  </description>
